t to find out more about the world of the Arisen!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/89-quatren","name":"Quatren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T02:45:30-07:00","id":1006,"title":"","content":"Oooh! While we've got you I have a few questions if you don't mind?<br /> <br /> Now that the game has been out in the wild for a while and we've got our first supplements what would be the one thing you'd change (or even just clarify) now that you've had a chance to see how the fan community has responded?<br /> <br /> What's the one thing you're really happy/proud/etc. of including in there?<br /> <br /> Some questions about the Ready Made Characters. The characters all seem to have Memory 3 (barring the one with a suspected misprint memory of 0) yet they seem to have strong personalities and ideas of who they are, where they come from and where they're going. Is that what Memory 3 is meant to look like? My interpretation from the Core book was that Memory led to a much more confused individual with chasms of missing history.<br /> <br /> Also, the vibe from the Character Pack was quite sleazy and vampirey with Judges hiding sexual indiscretions etc. Is that a tone you see the game being good for? Or in fact something intended? The characters seem like they'd fit right into a Vampire Coterie where everyone has just woken up from Torpor for a few generations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-nam